# DutyLog — Attendance & Salary Tracker

Single-file HTML app to track hourly attendance, OT, and leave, with automatic
salary calculation. Built to be wrapped into an Android APK using Capacitor.

File: `attendance_app.html`

---

## Features

- **Attendance tab**
  - Add entries as **Duty**, **Leave**, or **Emergency Leave**
  - Duty entries: In-time + Out-time → duty hours auto-calculated
  - OT hours entered manually per duty entry
  - Optional note per entry
  - Edit and delete any saved entry
- **Settings tab**
  - Set Hourly Rate (₹/hour)
  - Set separate OT Hourly Rate (₹/hour) — defaults to hourly rate if left blank
  - Export full backup as a `.json` file
  - Delete all data (with confirmation)
- **Summary tab**
  - Totals: duty days, total duty hours, total OT hours, leave days, emergency leave days, total salary
  - Full date-wise table: hours, OT, and ₹ salary per entry
  - Share button — sends a text summary via WhatsApp/any app (or copies to clipboard if sharing isn't supported)
- **Data storage**: everything is saved automatically in the device's local storage — no internet or server needed. Data stays on the phone even after closing the app.

---

## How salary is calculated

For each Duty entry:

```
duty hours = Out time − In time  (auto)
salary     = (duty hours × hourly rate) + (OT hours × OT rate)
```

Leave and Emergency Leave entries are counted separately in the totals but do not add to salary.

---

## Building the APK (Capacitor)

1. Install Node.js if not already installed.
2. Create a Capacitor project (one-time setup):
   ```
   npm init -y
   npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/android
   npm install -D @capacitor/cli
   npx cap init "DutyLog" "com.vks.dutylog" --web-dir=www
   ```
3. Copy the app into the web folder:
   ```
   mkdir www
   cp attendance_app.html www/index.html
   ```
4. Add the Android platform and sync:
   ```
   npx cap add android
   npx cap sync
   ```
5. Open in Android Studio and build the APK:
   ```
   npx cap open android
   ```
   In Android Studio: **Build → Build Bundle(s) / APK(s) → Build APK(s)**

The generated APK will be under `android/app/build/outputs/apk/`.

---

## Notes

- Package name used above (`com.vks.dutylog`) can be changed to whatever you prefer — keep it consistent if you rebuild later, or the app will install as a separate copy.
- App icon and splash screen can be set later using `npx cap` icon/splash tools or by replacing files under `android/app/src/main/res/`.
- To back up or move data to a new phone, use **Settings → Export Backup** to download the `.json` file.
